@ key bytes, pad byte (54 = ipad, 92 = opad) -> 64-character block for SHAC:
@ the key zero-padded to 64 bytes and XORed with the pad, with the bytes of each
@ 4-byte word reversed (SHAC reads words least significant nibble first).
\<< \-> k p
  \<<
    ""
    0 15 FOR w
      4 1 FOR j
        w 4 * j + \-> n
        \<<
          IF n k SIZE \<= THEN k n n SUB NUM ELSE 0 END
          R\->B p R\->B XOR B\->R CHR +
        \>>
      -1 STEP
    NEXT
  \>>
\>>
